+"""v7F under the PI's 2026-09-27 directive -- R1 (max speed: input + hard cap) and R4 (the
+tactical layer's behaviours and goals condition the operative plan).
+
+PI, verbatim: *"both of them should get the max speed, which it must not be exceeded ...
+All our tactical labels must be used to train the tactical layer to estimate and choose the
+right tactical behaviors and goals which MUST condition the operative planning."*
+
+WHAT IS UNDER TEST (all DEFAULT OFF; the default build/forward is pinned per tensor against
+the PRE-CHANGE ``v6.py`` -- content-anchored, never HEAD, the C75 rule):
+
+* R4  ``--tac-op-cond {off,detached,e2e}`` -> ``V6Stack.tac_op_port``: a ZERO-INIT
+  ``Linear(2*d_goal_embed -> d_goal_embed)`` projecting the LAT x LON behaviour posteriors
+  ``e_a_tac`` and ADDING them to ``e_g_tac`` before ``emit``. MEASURED at the tip
+  (``AUDIT_R4.md``): the goal reached the plan, the behaviours did NOT (the negative control
+  below re-executes that fact).
+* R1a ``--max-speed-input-v6`` -> ``V6Stack.vmax_tac``: the refcv6 4-bin one-hot through a
+  ZERO-INIT ``Linear(4 -> d_tac)`` ADDED to the planner-side tactical latent ``z_tac_p``.
+* R1b ``--plan-vmax-cap`` + ``emit(v_max=...)`` -> ``plan_speed_cap``: refav1's
+  ``_cap_speed`` semantics on EVERY candidate, before selection; every expectation below is a
+  hand-computed LITERAL, and the end-to-end case carries a DISCRIMINATING control (the same
+  emission WITHOUT the cap must exceed the limit, or the test proves nothing).
+
+The pre-change module: ``$TANITAD_V6_PRE_R1R4`` (a file path) when set, else the newest git
+revision of ``stack/tanitad/models/v6.py`` that does not carry ``tac_op_cond``; neither ->
+the byte-identity tests SKIP (a skipped test is honest, a self-comparison is not).
